<title>USA: U.S. court sees no ruling on FDA-tobacco this week.</title>
<headline>U.S. court sees no ruling on FDA-tobacco this week.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, North Carolina 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal judge weighing the tobacco industry's challenge to Food and Drug Administration (FDA) regulations on marketing and selling cigarettes in the United States will not rule until March 31 or later, the court said on Monday.</p>
<p>A taped message to advise lawyers and others awaiting U.S. District Court Judge William Osteen's ruling said no ruling would come until at least next Monday.</p>
<p>The judge has been considering the matter since February 10, when tobacco company lawyers asked the judge to throw out the FDA rules without a trial.</p>
<p>((-- Miami newsroom, 305-374-5013))</p>
